Package: RegCompassR
Title: Multiome Regulatory Evidence and Metabolic Reaction Analysis
Version: 2.4.19
Authors@R: c(person(given = "RegCompass", family = "Developers", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "dev@example.com"))
Author: RegCompass Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: RegCompass Developers <dev@example.com>
Description: Integrates paired single-cell RNA and ATAC regulatory evidence
    with genome-scale metabolic models for cell-type-resolved reaction analysis.
    The workflow provides condition-aware or standard Pando regulatory inference,
    multimodal SuperCell aggregation, reaction meta-modules, context-specific
    structural reconstruction, directional metabolic scoring, and post-analysis
    utilities. Stage 1 uses one parallel level at a time and memory-trimmed Pando
    working objects. Condition GRNs preserve Pando regulatory-domain, motif,
    peak-target-correlation and TF-target-correlation candidate logic. Candidate
    discovery is run on pooled eligible-condition cells and independently within
    each condition; exact target-TF-region triples passing the configured gates
    in either scope are deduplicated into one frozen common dictionary. Every
    condition is then fitted once on the same dictionary with a common-lambda
    no-fusion ridge model, retaining condition-specific comparable coefficients.
    Correlation support determines common-dictionary admission and is retained as
    provenance only; an edge is active within a fitted condition when that
    condition's ridge coefficient is estimable and BH-supported. Standard Pando
    uses the K=1 ridge route in RegCompass. Human standard and condition routes
    share the RegCompass default regulatory prior formed by the union of Pando's
    phastConsElements20Mammals.UCSC.hg38 and SCREEN.ccRE.UCSC.hg38 resources.
    Downstream regulatory eligibility requires a Pando BH-active edge, a valid
    target fit, and selected-lambda full-data target R-squared above the configured
    threshold. The target q state is one for evaluated supported regulation, zero
    for an evaluated target with no eligible edge, and missing only when the target
    was unavailable or not evaluated; R-squared is a gate rather than a multiplier.
    Stage 2 builds one multimodal WNN graph and one Walktrap hierarchy per broad
    cell type, selects condition-specific gamma-resolution cuts from that shared
    hierarchy, and locally repairs only undersized same-condition fragments along
    the same hierarchy while preserving the final metacell-count floor. Quantitative
    Layer 1 RNA is the equal-weight mean of single-cell linear CPM within the exact final
    SuperCell membership. Medium concentrations are provenance rather than implicit
    kinetics, and full-GEM medium cache identity is based on the final resolved
    reaction lower and upper bounds. Pando and SuperCell compatibility is checked
    from required runtime APIs and data contracts rather than package version
    strings; the Remotes entries target the current repository default branches.
    Mathematical and quantitative definitions are maintained in the package
    mathematical specification rather than duplicated in interface text.
